Ryujinx shader translator: texture offset emulation (InsertConstOffsets) for pool-indexed textures. GenerateBindlessAccess
gives such a texture operation two leading sources (texture index, then sampler index) and a separate sampler binding; the
emulation counted one leading source and built its textureQueryLod / textureSize / texture operations without the sampler,
so a bindless sample with a non-constant offset threw (Fire Emblem Fortune's Weave: 69 fragment blocks with TEX.SCR.B.AOFFI).
The derived operations now keep the sampler binding and index. Applied at build time by
translator/Ryujinx.Graphics.Shader.csproj to a copy under the build folder. The Ryujinx code in the context lines is MIT.
